{"id": "EUVD-2026-97016", "enisaUuid": "818aa4a2-6733-330b-a3e7-24983716757b", "description": "AmoyLab Unla through 0.10.0 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to obtain valid access tokens because the OAuth2 server never authenticates a resource owner. Attackers can register a client, request a code from /authorize, and exchange it at /token to access OAuth2-protected MCP prefixes, proxied upstream APIs and injected credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T13:26:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:48:20", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/amoylab-unla-oauth-self-issued-token-authz", "https://github.com/AmoyLab/Unla/blob/v0.10.0/internal/auth/oauth.go#L86-L147", "https://github.com/AmoyLab/Unla/blob/v0.10.0/internal/core/server.go#L229-L261", "https://github.com/AmoyLab/Unla", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/amoylab-unla-through-0.10.0-oauth2-authentication-bypass-via-authorize"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108865", "GHSA-pfxh-9349-4f24"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ad78f4f2-09dd-3af8-8cc3-d150092197ea", "product": {"name": "Unla", "vendor": {"name": "AmoyLab"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.10.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e31933e9-4352-351b-9691-26609643c59a", "vendor": {"name": "AmoyLab"}}], "isExploited": false}